    "background_story": "Evan was a skilled but reclusive archaeologist who spent most of his life exploring the depths of ancient ruins. His latest obsession was the long-abandoned city of Eldarath, hidden deep within a mist-shrouded valley. The air was perpetually damp, and the walls seemed to weep with moisture, but Evan was undeterred. He spent years excavating the site, uncovering secrets that had lain dormant for centuries. The damp conditions proved to be a blessing in disguise, as they helped preserve the delicate artifacts and texts that Evan discovered. His findings sparked a new wave of interest in the field, and Evan's name became synonymous with Eldarath. Despite the damp surroundings, Evan's passion for discovery burned bright, illuminating the dark recesses of history.",
